=== meta ===
rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: pytest.skip() added at the top of a conftest fixture disables every test that requests it
origin: issue #172 - the requested fixture in tests/conftest.py gained an unconditional `pytest.skip()` as its first statement while the test file stayed byte-identical; v0.4.2 (cfbefb8) reported zero findings of any severity. Runtime per the report (pytest 9.1.1): base `1 failed`, head `1 skipped`, exit 0
=== before: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest


@pytest.fixture
def items():
    return [{"price": 10.0, "qty": 3}, {"price": 5.0, "qty": 9}]
=== after: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest


@pytest.fixture
def items():
    pytest.skip("temporarily unavailable")
    return [{"price": 10.0, "qty": 3}, {"price": 5.0, "qty": 9}]
=== head: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def test_invoice_total(items):
    assert invoice_total(items) == 78.75
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "TEST_DISABLED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"], "path": "tests/conftest.py", "unit": "<suite>"}]
